Dependency mapping identifies the relationships between applications, servers, databases, storage systems, network components, and authentication services. Understanding these relationships is critical before migrating workloads to Azure.

A dependency map may identify:

* Application-to-server dependencies
* Application-to-database connections
* Server-to-server communication
* DNS dependencies
* Authentication dependencies
* Storage dependencies
* Network ports and protocols

For example, an application server may depend on a database server, an internal DNS server, and an authentication service. Migrating only the application server without considering these dependencies could cause the application to fail.

A real-life use case is an enterprise migrating a legacy application where several components communicate across an on-premises datacenter.

Dependency mapping allows migration teams to move related components in the correct sequence and minimize downtime.
